    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You're trapped in an infinite loop inside a movie theater trying to reach the right screening room.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Weird anomalies will occur. Spot them, run to get a new ticket, and keep going.</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>If it's safe, nothing unusual happens, get a new ticket.</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>If your answer is incorrect, you go back one ticket number.</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The Last Screening is a first-person horror anomaly-finding game set in a cinema venue.  You will play as Susie, a movie fanatic who has just received a ticket to watch a film she\u2019s been eagerly awaiting. Use your finest perception skills to help Susie get to her film. The first run we guarantee your safety; after that, you are on your own.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Monsters, jump scares, weird voices, blood... You better watch out because it's all coming for you.\u00a0\u00a0</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Ensure you don't miss any details to help Susie get to her movie on time.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The Last Screening is inspired by find-anomalies games that present liminal spaces and psychological horror walking simulators, like '<i>The Exit 8</i>', '<i>The Cabin Factory'</i>, '<i>Hospital 666'</i>, and the old goodie <i>'P.T.'.</i></p>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You're trapped in an infinite loop inside a movie theater trying to reach the right screening room.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Weird anomalies will occur. Spot them, run to get a new ticket, and keep going.</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>If it's safe, nothing unusual happens, get a new ticket.</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>If your answer is incorrect, you go back one ticket number.</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The Last Screening is a first-person horror anomaly-finding game set in a cinema venue.  You will play as Susie, a movie fanatic who has just received a ticket to watch a film she\u2019s been eagerly awaiting. Use your finest perception skills to help Susie get to her film. The first run we guarantee your safety; after that, you are on your own.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Monsters, jump scares, weird voices, blood... You better watch out because it's all coming for you.\u00a0\u00a0</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Ensure you don't miss any details to help Susie get to her movie on time.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The Last Screening is inspired by find-anomalies games that present liminal spaces and psychological horror walking simulators, like '<i>The Exit 8</i>', '<i>The Cabin Factory'</i>, '<i>Hospital 666'</i>, and the old goodie <i>'P.T.'.</i></p>",
    "short_description": "You find yourself inside a cinema hallway, ready to watch your film. The venue, however, has other plans for you.",
